  "id": "fundamental-symptoms",
  "term": "fundamental symptoms",
  "definition": "In historical psychopathology, fundamental symptoms are the underlying features of a mental disease that are present across all cases and support identifying the disease-process beneath changing outward symptoms. They are contrasted with shifting symptom pictures and are studied to distinguish the core disorder from its varied manifestations.",
